n hand, no pair or sequence possible with my other tiles), and it\u2019s relatively safe based on discard history.  \nW6/W7/W8 have potential to become pungs or pairs, improving hand value.  \nW9 is risky to discard since it\u2019s the last one and could give someone a pung, but keeping it has little use unless I draw the last W9 (unlikely). However, discarding W9 now could be dangerous because only 1 remains and someone might need it for honors/terminals pattern \u2014 but opponents\u2019 melds suggest less need for W9. Still, B3 is safer.  \n\nFinal choice: **Play B3**.  \n\n**Answer:** Play B3"}
